    "title": "Upper Burrell Township passes new zoning ordinance for data centers; residents express concerns - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By WPXI.com News Staff ,\n1 hours ago By WPXI Upper Burrell Township supervisors unanimously voted to approve a new zoning ordinance regulating data centers following a public hearing on Thursday.\nThe ordinance establishes formal standards regarding where data centers are permitted to operate within the municipality. It directly addresses key operational impacts, including regulations on noise levels, water use and local power supplies.\nDespite the enactment of the new regulations, local residents continue to express concerns regarding a proposed data center at the former ALCOA campus.\n“Something this size in our community should pay for the community,” one resident said.\nWith the zoning ordinance officially in place, township officials can now begin reviewing proposed data center plans submitted within the community.\nDownload the FREE WPXI News app for breaking news alerts.\nFollow Channel 11 News on Facebook and Twitter . | Watch WPXI NOW",
    "summary": "By WPXI.com News Staff , 1 hours ago By WPXI Upper Burrell Township supervisors unanimously voted to approve a new zoning ordinance regulating data centers following a public hearing on Thursday. The ordinance establishes formal standards regarding where data centers are permitted to operate within the municipality. It directly addresses key operational impacts, including regulations on noise levels, water use and local power supplies. Despite the enactment of the new regulations, local residents continue to express concerns regarding a proposed data center at the former ALCOA campus.",
